The 16-point accuracy gain costs 96 credits but only recovers 16 credits of marginal reward. Information-gathering only pays when the cost per unit of accuracy improvement is below the decision's reward delta — here it's 96/16 = 6 credits per percentage point, far exceeding the 1 credit per point breakeven.

